# Git workflow

The first bootstrap commit on `main` is historical. All later work uses this flow:

1. Start from an up-to-date `main`: `git checkout main && git pull`
2. Create a new branch named for the work (`feat/phase-2-ingestion`, `fix/...`, `chore/...`)
3. Commit only on that branch
4. Push the branch and open a PR into `main`
5. Merge into `main` only via that PR (or an explicit user request to merge)

Do not commit, amend, or push feature work directly on `main`.
Do not reuse one long-lived feature branch for unrelated phases.
